# gradlew.bat is the Gradle wrapper's Windows launcher script and must keep
# its native CRLF line endings (Windows batch files require CRLF to run
# correctly; converting it to LF would break the Windows wrapper). Without
# this attribute, `git diff --check` flags every CRLF line in the file as
# "trailing whitespace" (core.whitespace's default trailing-space rule does
# not special-case a CR immediately before the LF) even though the file's
# CRLF endings are intentional, not accidental whitespace. `cr-at-eol` tells
# git's whitespace checker to treat that trailing CR as part of the line
# terminator instead of stray trailing whitespace, without altering the
# file's actual bytes/line endings in any way.
gradlew.bat whitespace=cr-at-eol
